    "content_schema_version": 1,
    "content": {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Dividing integers"
        },
        {
          "type": "subheading",
          "text": "Dividing"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Division uses the same sign rules as multiplication. Divide the distances first. Then decide the sign. Same signs give a positive result. Different signs give a negative result."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet_list",
          "items": [
            "(-24) / (-6) = 4",
            "24 / (-6) = -4",
            "(-24) / 6 = -4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "image_asset": "lesson/lesson-2/sign-rules.png",
          "image_alt": "Sign rules chart for multiplication and division"
        },
        {
          "type": "subheading",
          "text": "Check with multiplication"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Division undoes multiplication. To check 24 / (-6) = -4, multiply back: (-4) x (-6) = 24."
        },
        {
          "type": "video",
          "video_code": "VID-INTEGER-MULTIPLY-DIVIDE",
          "segment_start_seconds": 45,
          "segment_end_seconds": 90
        },
        {
          "type": "worked_example",
          "title": "Choosing the sign",
          "problem": "Compute (-24) / (-6).",
          "steps": [
            "Step 1: Signs of (-24) / (-6) are the same. Result is positive.",
            "Step 2: 24 / 6 = 4."
          ],
          "answer": "Answer: 4."
        },
        {
          "type": "common_mistake",
          "text": "(-24) / 6 = 4 is wrong. The signs are different, so the answer is -4."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "variant": "cta",
          "text": "Ready to practice. Continue to the regular exercise for 6 questions."
        }
      ],
      "source_text": "Lesson 2.3 - Dividing integers\nSkill: S7\nObjective:\n1. Divide integers.\nDividing\nDivision uses the same sign rules as multiplication. Divide the distances first. Then decide the sign.\nSame signs -> positive\nDifferent signs -> negative\nExamples: (-24) / (-6) = 4. 24 / (-6) = -4. (-24) / 6 = -4.\nCheck with multiplication\nDivision undoes multiplication. To check 24 / (-6) = -4, multiply back: (-4) x (-6) = 24.\nWorked example\nProblem: Compute (-24) / (-6).\nStep 1: Signs of (-24) / (-6) are the same. Result is positive. Step 2: 24 / 6 = 4. Answer: 4.\nCommon mistake\n(-24) / 6 = 4 is wrong. The signs are different, so the answer is -4."
    }
  },
